   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system in Rockland county as the \"Jared Lloyd Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S8298",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8298-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-n, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8298\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system in Rockland county as the \"Jared Lloyd Memorial\nHighway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo rename a portion of the state highway system, in Rockland county, to\nhonor the memory of Spring Valley volunteer fire fighter Jared Lloyd.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill adds a new section, section 344-m, to the high-\nway law providing that the portion of state route forty-five, between\nNew Hempstead Road and East Eckerson Road in the town of Ramapo, as the\n\"Jared Lloyd Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection two requires the commissioner of transportation to provide for\nthe installation and maintenance of of adequate signing for the ceremo-\nnial renaming of the section of highway designated under section one of\nthe bill\n\nSection three provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn March 30th, 2021, volunteer firefighter Jared Llyod lost his life\nwhile responding to a massive fire at Evergreen Court, an assisted\nliving facility in the Village of Spring Valley. Renaming a portion of\nthe state highway system after Jared Lloyd is a small step toward ensur-\ning his loss and heroism is never forgotten.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
